  "query_preview": "..\nThe dry trade-wind regime has remained for the Marianas and looks to\ncontinue for the next few days, so isolated showers and mostly cloudy\nskies are expected for tonight, becoming partly cloudy Friday \nmorning. The northeasterly trades will continue easing up through \nFriday night before increasing the following day. Model guidance \ncontinues the drier trend for the Marianas through the next several \ndays before a potential shift in overall weather conditions over the \nweekend. As of now, models still show a wetter pattern with a slight\nchance of thunderstorms preamptively arriving on Guam first before \nspreading northward through the rest of the Marianas. However, \nuncertainty is high as models struggle to agree on the timing, \nlocation, and speed of a tropical disturbance that could form in \ncentral Micronesia and travel westward, bringing said weather \nconditions to the region. Satellite imagery does not indicate the \ndevelopment of a tropical disturbance in central Micronesia, so \nconfidence will remain low until such a system emerges. We will \ncontinue to monitor and communicate as the weekend nears.",
